As shown in the figure, there is a uniform electric field between two parallel metal plates A and B, with a distance of $10\mathrm{cm}$ between A and B. Points C and D are located within the electric field, with $CD=8\mathrm{cm}$, and the line segment CD forms a $60^{\circ}$ angle with the direction of the electric field. The distance from point C to plate A is $2\mathrm{cm}$. It is known that the work done by the electric field force when moving a proton from plate A to plate B is $4.0\times10^{-17}\mathrm{J}$. The charge of a proton is equal to the elementary charge, $e=1.6\times10^{-19}\mathrm{C}$. Find:
1. the electric field strength of the uniform electric field;
2. the potential difference between points C and D;
3. if plate B is grounded, the electric potential at point C;
4. if plate B is grounded, the electric potential energy of the proton at point C.
